From: ios-milanf-port (desk phase, 2026-10-25)
Subject: [PATCH] MILANF: survive having no IOStorageFamily at the root handoff

`iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp` carries three board gates and all three are about
one fact: sweet and milanf both run without IOStorageFamily, so neither
`IOMedia` nor `IOBlockStorageDriver` is a registered OS meta class. Sweet
taught the two affected functions to cope; the gates that teach them are
spelled `#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)`, so milanf takes Apple's arms
and both of Apple's arms assert.

Why this is a live stop and not a tidy-up: 0089 routes the root device through
sweet_ufs and `IOFindBSDRoot` jumps to its `iofrootx` label, which is the line
immediately above the first call -

    iofrootx:
        IOService::setRootMedia(service);

`setRootMedia()` looks up `IOBlockStorageDriver`, gets NULL, and under
`#else` (milanf today) reaches

    assert(ioblockstoragedriverClass);

`assert()` in `osfmk/kern/assert.h` is a real `__Panic`, not a DEVELOPMENT-only
no-op. So the first boot reaches the root handoff, prints `BSD root:
ufsroot0, major 3, minor 0` from 0089, and dies one line later with

    IOService.cpp:5200 Assertion failed: ioblockstoragedriverClass

`publishHiddenMedia()`, called from the tail of `setRootMedia()`, carries the
mirror-image assert under the opposite gate (`#if !defined(...SWEET)`), so
fixing only the first one just moves the panic eleven lines down to
`IOService.cpp:5130`.

Three edits, all the mechanical widening this series has used throughout:

| line | before | after |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 5129 | `#if !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)` | `&& !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)` |
| 5140 | `#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)` | `\|\| defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)` |
| 5191 | `#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)` | `\|\| defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)` |

The 5129 site is the only negated board gate in the entire tree, which makes it
the one place where `guards.py` reads backwards: a negated gate does not lose
milanf code, it *keeps* Apple code milanf cannot run. The inventory only tracks
lost code, so this class of site is invisible to it by construction - worth
knowing before trusting the remaining 26 sites as the complete worklist.

No new value is read off the DTB here and nothing board-specific is written:
both boards answer "no IOStorageFamily" the same way, so the widened arms are
the same arms. Comments are reworded board-neutrally, since "SWEET has no
IOStorageFamily" stops being true of the gate once milanf shares it.

Consequence worth stating because it changes what the code does: with
`ioblockstoragedriverClass` NULL, `setRootMedia()` sets `root = NULL`, walks
nothing, records `gIOServiceRootMediaParent = NULL` and hands that to
`publishHiddenMedia()`. There, `iomediaClass` is NULL too, `wasHiding` is
forced false, and `applyToInstances()` is skipped - so no service is ever
dereferenced through a missing meta class. The root vnode was already produced
by `sweet_ufs_rootdev()`; this call only maintains registry bookkeeping that
has nothing to track.

Verified without a compiler: fresh ci-art3, 0086-0094 applied one at a time in
order, every one exit 0, every touched file CR=0, patch CR=0. Link unverified;
CI in the morning.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
index 59c834e..a360c75 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -5126,7 +5126,7 @@ IOService::publishHiddenMedia(IOService * parent)
 	bool                wasHiding;
 
 	iomediaClass = OSMetaClass::getMetaClassWithName(gIOMediaKey);
-#if !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) && !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
 	assert(iomediaClass);
 #endif
 
@@ -5137,8 +5137,11 @@ IOService::publishHiddenMedia(IOService * parent)
 	}
 	UNLOCKNOTIFY();
 
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
-	/* SWEET has no IOStorageFamily: without the IOMedia class no media exists to unhide. */
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
+	/*
+	 * Neither board has IOStorageFamily: without the IOMedia class no
+	 * media exists to unhide.
+	 */
 	if (!iomediaClass) {
 		wasHiding = false;
 	}
@@ -5188,10 +5191,10 @@ IOService::setRootMedia(IOService * root)
 	bool unhide;
 
 	ioblockstoragedriverClass = OSMetaClass::getMetaClassWithName(gIOBlockStorageDriverKey);
-#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_MILANF)
 	/*
-	 * SWEET has no IOStorageFamily, so no service can be a block storage
-	 * driver: the root (e.g. a RAM disk) is not block media, as for image boot.
+	 * Neither board has IOStorageFamily, so no service can be a block
+	 * storage driver: the root is not block media, as for image boot.
 	 */
 	if (!ioblockstoragedriverClass) {
 		root = NULL;
